{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-2401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=4{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=8x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(8x)(\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})+(4{x}^{2})(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}) \\\\  & =8x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8da347f2f30eba8fa50ffb2ab7f31e8a8f3a44d00cd21ccd26c6898f38c1b4a2"} {"question" "q-2401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}+8x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}-x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "\\frac{8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{2x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}$ and the denominator $v(x)=2x.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=2.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}})(2x)-(\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x})(2)}{(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8da347f2f30eba8fa50ffb2ab7f31e8a8f3a44d00cd21ccd26c6898f38c1b4a2"} {"question" "q-2403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1+2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-2403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-9944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the slope of $f(x)={x}^{2}{sin}^{3}⁡x$ at $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-9944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nThis question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)={sin}^{3}⁡x.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2x)({sin}^{3}⁡x)+({x}^{2})(3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2x{sin}^{3}⁡x+3{x}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x})|}_{x=0} & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡(0)+3\\cdot {0}^{2}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-9944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8da347f2f30eba8fa50ffb2ab7f31e8a8f3a44d00cd21ccd26c6898f38c1b4a2"} {"question" "q-9944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-9944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-9944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-313371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{2x}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| ${y}^{′}$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $x{e}^{2x}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-313371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and the denominator $v(x)={e}^{2x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})({e}^{2x})-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(2{e}^{2x})}{{({e}^{2x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{x}-2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{({e}^{2x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{e}^{2x}-2x{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})}{{({e}^{2x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}(1-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{x{({e}^{2x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-313371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8da347f2f30eba8fa50ffb2ab7f31e8a8f3a44d00cd21ccd26c6898f38c1b4a2"} {"question" "q-313371" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-313371" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-2x\\ln(x)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-343354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=2x{e}^{6x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=($\n{{field-1}} $){e}^{6x}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-343354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=2x$ and $v(x)={e}^{6x}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=6{e}^{6x}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2)({e}^{6x})+(2x)(6{e}^{6x}) \\\\  & =(12x+2){e}^{6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-343354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8da347f2f30eba8fa50ffb2ab7f31e8a8f3a44d00cd21ccd26c6898f38c1b4a2"} {"question" "q-343354" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0ecbc7b070742a2065e3fc5e4688a6c42243799989475e40ccfa824f952778e"} {"question" "q-343354" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+12x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972470/state.js